<header class="page-head"><p class="eyebrow">REFERENCE LIBRARIES</p><h1>Deutsche Grammatik · A1 bis B1</h1><p class="dek">A searchable starting index linked to the course curriculum. Entries are expanded alongside the lessons that teach them.</p></header>
<label class="search-label" for="reference-search">Search grammar topics, verbs, vocabulary and expressions</label><input id="reference-search" type="search" placeholder="Try: Akkusativ, werden, Bewerbung…"><div class="reference-grid" id="reference-results">
{% for chapter in chapters %}<section class="reference-card" data-search="{{ chapter.grammar }} {{ chapter.title }}"><h2>{{ chapter.title }}</h2><p class="eyebrow">{{ chapter.level }}</p><p>{{ chapter.grammar }}</p><ul>{% for lesson in chapter.lessons %}<li>{% if lesson.id in completedLessons %}<a href="{{ ('/lessons/' + lesson.id + '/') | url }}">{{ lesson.id }} · {{ lesson.title }}</a>{% else %}{{ lesson.id }} · {{ lesson.title }}{% endif %}</li>{% endfor %}</ul></section>{% endfor %}</div>
<section><h2>Grammar handbook</h2><p><a href="{{ '/references/grammar/cases/' | url }}">The four German cases: functions, forms and decision steps</a> — a structured reference for nominative, accusative, dative and genitive.</p></section>
<section><h2>Past forms and temporal clauses</h2><p><a href="{{ '/references/grammar/past-narration/' | url }}">Perfekt, Präteritum, and temporal <em>als</em> and <em>wenn</em></a> — principal rules, patterns and links to L10–L12.</p></section>
<section><h2>Verb atlas</h2><p><a href="{{ '/verbs/' | url }}">Search verb principal parts</a> — an initial 34-entry A2 set with present form, Präteritum, Partizip II, auxiliary, usage pattern and example.</p></section>
<section><h2>Current coverage</h2><p>The verb atlas is being expanded alongside lessons. A complete A1–B1 verb inventory, thematic vocabulary library and expressions handbook remain to be authored. No final coverage count is inferred from the curriculum map.</p></section>
